        "title": "feat(ui): show estimated run cost in context popover",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe context popover shows current context and latest-run token usage, but omits estimated run cost even when the Gateway already exposes it.\n\nRelated: #100264\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis reads the existing optional `estimatedCostUsd` session field and renders it as an `Est. cost` stat. The stat is omitted when unavailable; finite non-negative values, including zero, use the existing USD formatter. No Gateway protocol change.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can see estimated run cost beside input and output tokens from the chat context ring, without an invented value for sessions or providers that do not expose cost.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox via Crabbox: `tbx_01kwsg0z2ja49hdbgkxq6h39wz` (`violet-shrimp`).\n- `pnpm test ui/src/pages/chat/chat-composer.test.ts`: 8 passed.\n- `pnpm test:ui:e2e ui/src/e2e/chat-flow.e2e.test.ts`: 20 passed.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:check`: 20 locales clean, zero fallbacks.\n- `pnpm check:changed`: passed.\n- `pnpm ui:build`: passed.\n- Exact-head post-rebase rerun: unit, mocked browser E2E, and i18n checks passed at `5c1ba3fd46902960a92ba9579a78a97c73c5ed09`.\n- Fresh autoreview: no actionable findings, confidence 0.97.\n- Screenshot gap: the selected Chrome profile does not have the Codex Chrome Extension available, so existing-profile visual capture was blocked and no isolated-browser fallback was used. The mocked real-browser E2E covers the visible cost row.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
